.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt OPENSSL-REHASH 1ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm openssl-rehash ,
.Nm c_rehash
.Nd Create symbolic links to files named by the hash values
.Sh SYNOPSIS =for openssl duplicate options
.Sy openssl
.Sy rehash
.Pf [ Sy -h ]
.Pf [ Sy -help ]
.Pf [ Sy -old ]
.Pf [ Sy -compat ]
.Pf [ Sy -n ]
.Pf [ Sy -v ]
.Pf [ Sy -provider
.Em name ]
.Pf [ Sy -provider-path
.Em path ]
.Pf [ Sy -provparam
.Em [name:]key=value ]
.Pf [ Sy -propquery
.Em propq ]
.Pf [ Em directory ]
\&...
.Pp
.Sy c_rehash
.Pf [ Sy -h ]
.Pf [ Sy -help ]
.Pf [ Sy -old ]
.Pf [ Sy -n ]
.Pf [ Sy -v ]
.Pf [ Sy -provider
.Em name ]
.Pf [ Sy -provider-path
.Em path ]
.Pf [ Sy -provparam
.Em [name:]key=value ]
.Pf [ Sy -propquery
.Em propq ]
.Pf [ Em directory ]
\&...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This command is generally equivalent to the external script
.Sy c_rehash ,
except for minor differences noted below.
.Pp
.Sy openssl rehash
scans directories and calculates a hash value of each
.Pa .pem ,
.Pa .crt ,
.Pa .cer ,
or
.Pa .crl
file in the specified directory list and creates symbolic links for each
file, where the name of the link is the hash value.
(If the platform does not support symbolic links, a copy is made.)
This command is useful as many programs that use OpenSSL require
directories to be set up like this in order to find certificates.
.Pp
If any directories are named on the command line, then those are
processed in turn.
If not, then the
.Sy SSL_CERT_DIR
environment variable is consulted; this should be a colon-separated list
of directories, like the Unix
.Sy PATH
variable.
If that is not set then the default directory (installation-specific but
often
.Pa /usr/local/ssl/certs )
is processed.
.Pp
In order for a directory to be processed, the user must have write
permissions on that directory, otherwise an error will be generated.
.Pp
The links created are of the form
.Em HHHHHHHH.D ,
where each
.Em H
is a hexadecimal character and
.Em D
is a single decimal digit.
When a directory is processed, all links in it that have a name in that
syntax are first removed, even if they are being used for some other
purpose.
To skip the removal step, use the
.Sy -n
flag.
Hashes for CRL's look similar except the letter
.Sy r
appears after the period, like this:
.Em HHHHHHHH. Ns Sy r Ns Em D .
.Pp
Multiple objects may have the same hash; they will be indicated by
incrementing the
.Em D
value.
Duplicates are found by comparing the full SHA-1 fingerprint.
A warning will be displayed if a duplicate is found.
.Pp
A warning will also be displayed if there are files that cannot be
parsed as either a certificate or a CRL or if more than one such object
appears in the file.
.Ss Script Configuration
The
.Sy c_rehash
script uses the
.Sy openssl
program to compute the hashes and fingerprints.
If not found in the user's
.Sy PATH ,
then set the
.Sy OPENSSL
environment variable to the full pathname.
Any program can be used, it will be invoked as follows for either a
certificate or CRL:
.Bd -literal
  $OPENSSL x509 -hash -fingerprint -noout -in FILENAME
  $OPENSSL crl -hash -fingerprint -noout -in FILENAME
.Ed
.Pp
where
.Em FILENAME
is the filename.
It must output the hash of the file on the first line, and the
fingerprint on the second, optionally prefixed with some text and an
equals sign.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy -help Sy -h
Display a brief usage message.
.It Sy -old
Use old-style hashing (MD5, as opposed to SHA-1) for generating links to
be used for releases before 1.0.0. Note that current versions will not
use the old style.
.It Sy -n
Do not remove existing links.
This is needed when keeping new and old-style links in the same
directory.
.It Sy -compat
Generate links for both old-style (MD5) and new-style (SHA1) hashing.
This allows releases before 1.0.0 to use these links along-side newer
releases.
.It Sy -v
Print messages about old links removed and new links created.
By default, this command only lists each directory as it is processed.
.It Sy -provider Em name
.It Sy -provider-path Em path
.It Sy -provparam Em [name:]key=value
.It Sy -propquery Em propq
See
.Xr openssl 1 ,
.Xr provider 7 ,
and
.Xr property 7 .
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy OPENSSL
The path to an executable to use to generate hashes and fingerprints
(see above).
.It Sy SSL_CERT_DIR
Colon separated list of directories to operate on.
Ignored if directories are listed on the command line.
.El
